<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip Sigismund of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1568">1568</a>–<a href="/years/1623">1623</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip Sigismund of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfenbuttel">Wolfenbüttel</a> was a Lutheran prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">House of Welf</a> who administered the prince-bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verden">Verden</a> from 1586 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osnabruck">Osnabrück</a> from 1591 until his death in 1623. As administrator he consolidated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in Verden, where Lutheran rulers had replaced the earlier Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-sigismund-of-brunswick-wolfenbuttel.jpg" alt="Philip Sigismund of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PhilippSigismundBraunschweig.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
